    "body": "I’m unsure where the draft spec for `ImageDecoder.isTypeSupported` lives, so apologies if this is the wrong place to post. But I noticed that the flagged Chromium implementation is promise-based, which seems confusingly different from `isTypeSupported` on `MediaSource` which synchronously returns a boolean. https://github.com/dalecurtis/image-decoder-api/issues/6 Can we not make `ImageDecoder.isTypeSupported` synchronously return a boolean as well? Or is it somehow expensive to check whether a given image type is supported?",
